    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d973">

                <pb facs="1303" n="1179" xml:id="pg1179"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">467.11 W 89/32: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-10-27T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 27,
                                1923—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>200. Your 271 October 18, 11 a.m.</p>
                <p>For Bristol.</p>
                <p>Under date of October 24, by direction of the President, you were granted two
                    full powers to negotiate, conclude and sign with Turkey (1) a Claims Convention
                    (2) a Naturalization Convention.</p>
                <p>These documents<anchor n="41" xml:id="d973-f1"/> are being forwarded by mail.
                    Should it become necessary their contents can be telegraphed. It is understood,
                    of course, that no action will be taken under these full powers without the
                    Department’s definite instruction.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
